WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.826
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.730
SPEAKER: Looking to create
an event-driven app?

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.300
Give me a minute and I'll show
you how, using Cloud Functions.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.670
Cloud Functions is an
event-driven, serverless

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:18.330
compute platform with scales
automatically based on load.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.400
And you're only billed
while the code is running,

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.340
so if your function is
idle, the cost is zero.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:24.360
It's easy to set up.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.090
Just write your logic in any
of the supporting languages

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:29.370
and trigger it
via HTTP requests.

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:32.430
File uploads to Cloud
Storage, Events, and Pub/Sub,

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:33.680
or Firebase.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.770
It offers built-in security at
role and at per-function level.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.500
You can also observe and
diagnose your applications

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.900
using the Operations tools.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.360
Cloud Functions acts
as a building block.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.790
You can build real-time
data processing apps,

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:51.090
like bringing in IoT
device data for analysis,

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:53.670
calling machine learning
APIs to extract information

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:57.450
and images, texts, or videos
as soon as the file is uploaded

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:00.750
to Cloud Storage, creating
conversational experiences

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.500
with Dialogflow, and
even creating serverless

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.980
back ends using Firebase
and third-party apps.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:09.750
Next time you're looking to
create an event-driven app,

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:12.000
take a minute and look
at Cloud Functions.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.980
To learn more, check out
cloud.google.com/functions.

